1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,527
I've been living in Estonia for about a year

2
00:00:01,527 --> 00:00:03,287
now and people always say this place is the

3
00:00:03,287 --> 00:00:05,527
digital hub of Europe or something like that.

4
00:00:05,527 --> 00:00:06,957
And I'm not going to lie,

5
00:00:06,957 --> 00:00:07,727
it's so real.

6
00:00:07,727 --> 00:00:09,507
Everything you want to do here is online.

7
00:00:09,507 --> 00:00:10,727
I'm not exaggerating.

8
00:00:10,727 --> 00:00:12,307
Everything. Your health records.

9
00:00:12,307 --> 00:00:13,467
Everything links so well.

10
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:15,067
There is nothing you want to do that you

11
00:00:15,067 --> 00:00:16,207
can't do online here.

12
00:00:16,207 --> 00:00:17,247
You can get married online,

13
00:00:17,247 --> 00:00:19,087
you can divorce online.

14
00:00:19,087 --> 00:00:20,867
There's a link for everything you want to do

15
00:00:20,867 --> 00:00:21,767
in Estonia.

16
00:00:21,767 --> 00:00:24,887
The data ecosystem that the governments use,

17
00:00:24,887 --> 00:00:25,747
that they run here,

18
00:00:25,747 --> 00:00:27,017
the way it syncs,

19
00:00:27,017 --> 00:00:28,807
I genuinely admire it.

20
00:00:28,807 --> 00:00:30,187
And as someone coming from Nigeria,

21
00:00:30,187 --> 00:00:31,767
it blew my mind when I got here,

22
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:32,907
where everything just syncs.

23
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:34,947
And I see Ghana doing something in this

24
00:00:34,947 --> 00:00:36,587
direction. My first instinct is like,

25
00:00:36,587 --> 00:00:37,047
yes, please,

26
00:00:37,047 --> 00:00:37,547
more of this.

27
00:00:37,547 --> 00:00:39,047
Because it solves so much problems.

28
00:00:39,047 --> 00:00:40,627
There's one reliable record instead of like

29
00:00:40,627 --> 00:00:42,457
just pieces of paper everywhere.

30
00:00:42,457 --> 00:00:44,833
Instead of NIN and this and that.
